This shouldn't be needed as the "device_is_ready" function allows NULL to be passed, but I see there is a pointer dereference that could be a problem.

You can do instead:

<pre>
if (!device_is_ready(data->adc)) {
	LOG_ERR("ADC device is not ready");
	return -ENODEV;
}
</pre>

then `if (data->adc == NULL) ` can be removed.
